Block definitions (advanced)
What a block looks like and how it exports are all written in [code]blocks/{language}/*.xml[/code] —
[b]adding a block needs no code[/b]:

[code]<Block name="Print">
  <Literal>print</Literal>
  <Field id="content" />
  <Row>
	<Text>Print</Text>
	<LineBox id="content" placeholder="frog" />
  </Row>
</Block>[/code]

[ul]
[*][code]<Literal>[/code] / [code]<Field>[/code]: the export template (output as-is / read the value of a field);
[*][code]<Field id="target" link="true"/>[/code]: this slot stores a [b]block reference[/b] (this is what Jump's target is);
[*][code]<Field as="string"/>[/code]: a string slot (quotes and escaping are handled by the editor, so typing quotes in the content will not break it);
[*][code]<Field allow_empty="true"/>[/code]: allow an empty value (comment text);
[*][code]<Item alias="atan2">angle</Item>[/code]: recognize the old name (import automatically converts it to the current spelling);
[*][code]<Place when="…" after="another element id"/>[/code] (or [code]before=[/code]): written inside an element, it moves that element before/after another element when the condition holds — blocks whose order changes with the option (such as a unary operation needing [code]result = not a[/code]) rely on it, so you do not have to write the field twice;
[*][code]<Row when="…">[/code]: an explicit row break; [code]when[/code] supports [code]&[/code] (and), [code]|[/code] (or), [code]~[/code] (not) and parentheses;
[*]The elements are [code]<Text>[/code] / [code]<LineBox>[/code] / [code]<Option>[/code]+[code]<Item>[/code] / [code]<Button>[/code] / [code]<Selector>[/code] / [code]<JumpTarget>[/code] / [code]<Nest>[/code].
[/ul]

Misspelled field names, invalid values and unregistered element tags are all reported when loading — a mistake never silently becomes "always shown".